==Food self-sufficiency and price stabilization==

The central strategic objective of MAFF under the Ikazaki Cabinet is elevating the national calorie-based food self-sufficiency ratio from its historic trough of 38 percent toward a statutory target of 50 percent by 2035. The Crop Production Bureau administers the Direct Income Support Scheme for Farmers (農業者戸別所得補償制度), transferring direct deficiency payments to family farms when market prices drop below average production costs.

Concurrently, the Fisheries Agency enforces Total Allowable Catch (TAC) limits across domestic ocean waters, balancing marine conservation with the economic survival of coastal fishing ports. Following regional maritime disruptions in late 2026, the Fisheries Agency deployed enhanced patrol cutters to safeguard domestic trawlers operating in contested fishing grounds within the East Fosian Sphere.

==Intergovernmental relations with prefectural and metropolitan governments==

Agricultural, forestry, and marine resource policies in Okaiken are executed through continuous, institutional partnerships between MAFF, the forty-seven provincial prefectures, and [[Okami Metropolis]]. Because climatic zones and soil topographies range from northern snow belts to southern sub-tropical archipelagos, agricultural administration cannot be managed effectively through rigid central mandates.

The ministry projects its statutory presence into the regions through seven Regional Agricultural Administration Offices (地方農政局). These regional offices work in direct liaison with Prefectural Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (農林水産部). At the municipal level, statutory land-use regulation is exercised by local Agricultural Committees (農業委員会), composed of local farmers and legal experts elected or appointed under prefectural oversight. These committees hold statutory authority to approve or deny the conversion of designated farmland into commercial real estate, preventing speculative corporate land grabs and preserving prime agrarian acreage in prefectures such as [[Miyagi Prefecture]] and [[Yamagata Prefecture]].

In forestry and watershed management, MAFF's Forestry Agency coordinates with prefectural forestry divisions to manage national and private forests. Watershed protection forests (水源涵養保安林) situated in mountainous prefectures provide drinking water and flood protection for downstream urban metropolises. The central ministry provides extensive National Forest Management Subsidies to prefectures, funding the thinning of overgrown cedar plantations and preventing fatal landslides during typhoon seasons.

Relations with the [[Okami Metropolitan Government]] center on the vital logistics of feeding the capital's massive urban population. While Okami Metropolis maintains active agricultural zones in the western Tama hills and greenhouse horticulture on the Izu Islands, the primary administrative interface between MAFF and the capital is the Okami Central Wholesale Market network, including the flagship Toyosu and Ota wholesale terminals. MAFF food safety inspectors collaborate directly with the Okami Metropolitan Bureau of Industrial and Labor Affairs and municipal public health veterinarians, inspecting daily seafood, livestock, and produce auctions that process thousands of tons of foodstuffs arriving from provincial prefectures each morning.

